course: dictionary
lesson: 2642
title: Detect: noticing what is hard to see
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To detect something means to notice or discover it, often when it is hard to see, hear or smell. A machine can detect things too. «Automatic doors use sensors to detect people coming, and motors open them.» The sensors notice someone walking closer, so the door knows to open.
explain: Detect is a verb, so it changes: detects, detected, detecting. Related words include detector (a tool that finds things) and detective (someone who looks for clues). In «Sweden detected the radiation on 28 April», Sweden found something that was hard to notice on its own.
explain: Use the context to check your meaning. «Menthol in mint switches on the nerve sensors that detect cold, so the mouth feels cool though it is not colder.» Ask: what do the sensors notice? They notice cold. Then swap in your meaning for detect and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Detect means to notice or discover something that is hard to see, hear or smell.
fact: Detect can also mean to find something using a special tool or test, such as «detect metal».
fact: Detect is a verb: detects, detected and detecting show when it happens.
fact: «Virus detected!» means a computer program has found a virus.
fact: Smoke detectors and carbon monoxide alarms detect danger so people can get out in time.
exercise: «Menthol in mint switches on the nerve sensors that detect cold, so the mouth feels cool though it is not colder.» What does detect mean here? | *Notice or sense | Taste sweet | Hide from | Make warmer
exercise: «Sweden detected the radiation on 28 April, before Moscow announced it.» What does detected mean? | Ignored it | *Found or discovered it | Cooked it | Forgot about it
exercise: Which word means a tool that finds things? | *Detector | Dentist | Detour | Dinner
test: Which of these would a smoke alarm do? | *Detect smoke | Sleep all night | Sing a song | Paint the walls
test: What does detect most nearly mean in «Automatic doors use sensors to detect people coming»? | *Notice people coming | Ask people to leave | Hide people | Turn off the lights
exam: Which word could replace detected in «The detective ___ a tiny clue under the rug» without changing the meaning? | *Spotted | Hid | Dropped | Ignored
